# Mode 2 build -- commit the code, docs and small result artifacts; shed the
# large, reproducible outputs (workspace RETENTION.md: "is this the only copy of
# a *result*, or is it *reproducible*?").
#
# KEPT (the evidence): every eval_val.json / eval_test.json / model.json,
# compare_summary__*.json, artifacts/{audit,splits/*/split_report.json,triage,
# controls,ablations,clip,tuning}, all pipeline_*/ code, all stage*.py, the docs,
# results.csv / pipelines_overview.csv / pipeline_catalog.csv, logs/*.sh.
#
# SHED (regenerable from the code + config): trained model binaries and the
# feature/split caches. The repo-root .gitignore already drops *.parquet, *.txt,
# *.pt and *.log; these lines add the formats it does not catch.
*.ubj
*.pkl
*.bin
*.joblib
artifacts/features/

# --- KEEP despite the repo-root .gitignore ----------------------------------
# It blanket-ignores *.csv and README.md; these three CSVs and this folder's
# README are build deliverables, not dataset files.
!results.csv
!pipelines_overview.csv
!pipeline_catalog.csv
!README.md

# Saved prediction arrays (tests_*/ and tests_tabnet/build/): regenerable from
# the recorded seeds, and up to 176 MB each. Their sha256 is pinned in the
# model.json of any arm that replays them.
*.npz

# TabNet model archives (5 MB each): regenerable, bitwise, with train_tabnet_pred.py (2026-09-27 check); in the backup set.
*.zip
wx_cache/
tests_newdata/points/
tests_newdata/points_est/
